config X58_PRO_E_B06M_BASEINIT
	bool "Enable B06M one-channel baseinit experiment"
	depends on X58_PRO_E_BRINGUP_STAGE = 11
	default n
	help
	  Add an explicitly armed baseinit command for the exact E5645, Slow-QPI,
	  DDR-ratio-6, channel-2, dual-rank SPD-0x54 configuration proven during
	  B06J-HW-01.  It uses vendor-observed policy values, bounded RCOMP/ZQCL
	  polls, and serialized UART markers between DIMM-reset phases.  It does
	  not explicitly wait for the final character to reach TEMT; B06N adds
	  that corrected timing path.  It neither sets MC_CONTROL.INIT_DONE nor
	  accesses ordinary DRAM or SPI flash.

config X58_PRO_E_B06N_TIMED_MRS
	bool "Enable B06N measured MRS timing"
	depends on X58_PRO_E_B06M_BASEINIT
	default n
	help
	  Preserve B06M while adding an explicit UART-TEMT delay after every
	  DDR3 MRS command.  At 115200 baud each transmitted progress byte takes
	  about 86.8 microseconds, conservatively exceeding the vendor's observed
	  one-microsecond wait without assuming a TSC frequency.  Reset phase
	  markers also receive an explicit bounded TEMT completion check.

config X58_PRO_E_B06V0_VENDOR_INIT
	bool "Enable B06V0 local MSI vendor-init probe"
	depends on X58_PRO_E_BRINGUP_STAGE = 11
	depends on ARCH_ROMSTAGE_X86_32
	default n
	help
	  Add a default-off, explicitly armed research path for locally extracted
	  MSI A7522IMS.8F0 CSI_INITDLL and MINITDLL code.  No proprietary bytes
	  are part of the coreboot source or ordinary coreboot image; a separate
	  hash-pinned local composition step places them at their original XIP
	  addresses.  The ROM monitor verifies every complete inserted range,
	  entry metadata, exact SPD topology, and the CAR scratch layout before
	  permitting a manual call.  It never calls either
	  module automatically and never continues to ramstage or a payload.

	  This option disables the pre-RAM CBFS metadata cache to leave bounded
	  CAR space for the vendor state, workspace, guarded stack, and result
	  snapshot.  It also loads and requires the CPUID-206c2 Intel microcode
	  revision 0x1f before CAR.  The path is restricted to the current
	  E5645/sole-SPD-0x54 lab configuration and is not a native X58
	  memory-init implementation.

config X58_PRO_E_B06V1_REG_SCRIPT
	bool "Enable B06V1 transactional register scripting"
	depends on X58_PRO_E_B06V0_VENDOR_INIT
	default n
	help
	  Add a bounded pre-DRAM register-script engine to the B06V0 ROM monitor.
	  A script can contain up to 32 read, write, mask, poll, pause-delay, and
	  assert operations over I/O, PCI configuration, MMIO, and MSR spaces.
	  The table must first be sealed; execution then requires a separate
	  one-shot SCRIPT arm and the exact digest of the complete operation table.
	  Every step is logged before and after access; polling and delay loops have
	  hard limits.  Scripted memory writes overlapping CAR are rejected.

	  Writes explicitly marked reversible retain their prior values.  Manual
	  rollback and rollback-on-failure replay those values in reverse order,
	  but cannot undo write-once fields, W1C semantics, triggered side effects,
	  resets, a stopped CPU, or a lost QPI link.  This remains an experimental
	  recovery-lab feature and performs no operation automatically at boot.

config X58_PRO_E_B06V2_CSI_HEADER_FIX
	bool "Identify the corrected CSI-header build as B06V2"
	depends on X58_PRO_E_B06V1_REG_SCRIPT
	default n
	help
	  Give the B06V1 transactional monitor a distinct B06V2 identity after
	  correcting the CSI_INITDLL DOS e_lfanew gate from the disproven 0x80
	  value to the measured, hash-pinned 0xb0 value.  This option changes no
	  automatic execution policy: CSI and MINIT remain separately armed and
	  the firmware remains terminal in CAR.

config X58_PRO_E_B06V3_WARM_RESUME
	bool "Accept the exact post-CSI I801 state as B06V3"
	depends on X58_PRO_E_B06V2_CSI_HEADER_FIX
	default n
	help
	  Permit romstage to continue after a reset only when the ICH10R SMBus
	  function is already in the exact state programmed by this firmware:
	  BAR4 0x401, HOSTC 0x01, and PCI command 0x0001.  The original cold
	  tuple remains accepted and every other tuple still fails closed.

	  This is an observation aid for the reset deliberately triggered by the
	  locally supplied MSI CSI module.  It does not automatically call CSI,
	  MINIT, or any register script, and it does not claim that RAM or QPI has
	  been initialized.

config X58_PRO_E_B06V4_POLICY_TELEMETRY
	bool "Enable B06V4 MSI policy-input telemetry"
	depends on X58_PRO_E_B06V3_WARM_RESUME
	default n
	help
	  Add a read-only report of the two distinct CMOS banks used by the
	  original MSI MINIT wrapper and of ICH10 ALT_GP_SMI_EN.  Correct the
	  experimental policy builder to follow the original wrapper's
	  CMOS-diagnostic-invalid path: extended CMOS byte 0x8e is bounded in
	  the generated policy without writing CMOS, while optional CMOS-derived
	  policy fields remain zero when the standard diagnostic byte is invalid.

	  The valid-CMOS path remains restricted to the previously captured
	  field-6:4 value 1 profile because its other branches are not yet fully
	  reconstructed.  This option does not automatically call CSI or MINIT,
	  write CMOS data, or access ordinary DRAM.

config X58_PRO_E_B06V5_COLD_MINIT
	bool "Enable B06V5 explicit cold-MINIT policy experiment"
	depends on X58_PRO_E_B06V4_POLICY_TELEMETRY
	default n
	help
	  Add a separately armed vpolicy cold command restricted to the exact
	  returned CSI tuple EAX/EBX/ECX = 2/2/0x106 and the exact B06V4 policy
	  candidate that returned with EAX=0 and workspace bytes 1/2 both zero.
	  Static analysis and B06V4 hardware evidence show that the original
	  status-derived policy bit 18 is copied to MINIT workspace byte 0x4f bit
	  2, causing MINIT to return after phase B3 without running phases B4
	  through B8.  The command clears that bit and the policy status byte to
	  test the explicit hypothesis that the isolated coreboot path must request
	  a cold initialization rather than the vendor wrapper's unresolved
	  multi-pass/recovery path.

	  This override is not automatic, is marked as a modified policy, and
	  still requires the normal full-policy digest installation and separate
	  MINIT arm.  A returned call reports MINIT's internal completion marker
	  and selected Uncore registers but never accesses ordinary DRAM.

config X58_PRO_E_B06V6_AUTO_HANDOFF
	bool "Enable B06V6 automatic fixed-configuration RAM-init handoff"
	depends on X58_PRO_E_B06V5_COLD_MINIT
	depends on CONSOLE_SERIAL && DRIVERS_UART_8250IO
	depends on !OVERRIDE_UART_FOR_CONSOLE && UART_FOR_CONSOLE = 0
	depends on !UART_OVERRIDE_BAUDRATE && CONSOLE_SERIAL_115200
	depends on TTYS0_LCS = 3
	depends on !DRIVERS_UART_8250IO_SKIP_INIT
	depends on !NO_XIP_EARLY_STAGES && BOOT_DEVICE_MEMORY_MAPPED
	default n
	help
	  Automatically replay only the hardware-observed B06V5 path for the
	  exact E5645, sole-SPD-0x54, Slow-QPI, DDR-ratio-6 configuration.  Every
	  complete SPD, CSI-state, policy and MINIT-workspace digest and the
	  selected post-MINIT Uncore registers must match the recorded values.
	  Any mismatch returns to the interactive CAR ROM monitor.

	  CSI is a two-pass operation.  The automatic transaction must start from
	  the exact cold-default I801 tuple.  Before the first call this experiment
	  puts a five-byte, complemented volatile signature in the idle I801 host
	  registers; only the exact configured-I801 reset continuation with the
	  complete retained signature may make the second call.  A distinct
	  in-progress signature blocks a third automatic call if CSI or MINIT resets
	  unexpectedly.  Signature retention is an explicit hardware hypothesis: if
	  it is not retained by the observed configured-I801 continuation, the path
	  falls back to ROMMON.  A second marker uses bit 7 of the exact observed
	  CMOS diagnostic byte 0x0e (0x6c -> 0xec); both values select the same
	  reverse-engineered MSI diagnostic-invalid policy branch.  This marker also
	  prevents a reset which restores complete I801 cold defaults from starting
	  pass one again.  It is restored only after exact MINIT success.  A failed
	  run therefore needs the separately armed ROMMON "autoguard clear" command
	  followed by an AC power cycle before another automatic attempt.

	  Any marker write or readback failure stops and requires CMOS clear or
	  external recovery rather than leaving an ambiguous reset path.

	  On an exact MINIT return this option returns from board romstage so the
	  normal coreboot post-CAR/ramstage path can continue.  The locally composed
	  vendor modules remain non-redistributable research inputs; this option
	  adds no proprietary bytes and is not native X58 memory initialization.

config X58_PRO_E_B06V7_ROBUST_SLOWQPI
	bool "Enable B06V7 robust Slow-QPI automatic RAM-init handoff"
	depends on X58_PRO_E_B06V6_AUTO_HANDOFF
	default n
	help
	  Keep the complete B06V6 automatic, reset-guarded Slow-QPI path, but
	  recognize two hardware-observed classes of bytes which vary across
	  otherwise successful runs.  CSI state byte 0x2a6 must be exactly 0x08
	  or 0x0c and is zeroed only for a canonical-state digest.  Nine bounded,
	  hardware-derived MINIT workspace ranges are likewise zeroed only for a
	  canonical-workspace digest.  The raw buffers are never modified, and
	  both raw and canonical digests are retained in the version-2 handoff.

	  CPU, microcode, sole SPD at 0x54, policy, CSI register tuple, Slow-QPI
	  Uncore state, MTRRs, and destructive DRAM gates remain identical to
	  B06V6.  The independently observed High-QPI CSI state does not pass the
	  canonical Slow-QPI digest.  This option is a separate default-off
	  experiment and does not generalize DIMM, CPU, QPI, or memory policy.

config X58_PRO_E_B06V8_HIGH_QPI_3PASS
	bool "Enable B06V8 experimental High-QPI three-pass CSI probe"
	depends on X58_PRO_E_B06V7_ROBUST_SLOWQPI
	default n
	help
	  Add a separate, terminal three-pass CSI experiment for the exact E5645,
	  sole-SPD-0x54, DDR-ratio-6 lab configuration.  Pass one uses CSI's
	  internal SYRE reset.  Pass two accepts only the hardware-observed logical
	  return tuple and paired CPU/IOH pre-reset state, then emits the exact MSI
	  IOH SYRE edge sequence once.  Pass three requires the complete observed
	  High-QPI endpoint state, invokes CSI once, records raw state and endpoint
	  telemetry if it returns, and always remains in the CAR ROM monitor.

	  This option never invokes MINIT and never hands off to postcar, ramstage,
	  or a payload.  The explicit live High-QPI authorization 0x2c at standard
	  CMOS byte 0x0e is changed to the in-progress value 0xec, and three distinct
	  retained I801 signatures form a one-shot phase/retry guard; any ambiguous
	  state fails closed.  The outer
	  QPI reset uses IOH 00:14.2 CC bit 10 and never CF9.  The I801 signature
	  retention across that outer reset is still an untested hardware
	  hypothesis.

	  B06V8 additionally requires a deterministic one-byte branch patch in the
	  local, user-supplied MSI CSI wrapper.  It forces the complete CMOS-input
	  parser even while the persistent standard-CMOS guard is 0xec; exact
	  read-only extended-CMOS inputs 80/81/82/88/89=b3/19/d7/67/cb are required
	  before every call.  No extended-CMOS data is written.  Neither the patched
	  wrapper nor any other proprietary bytes may be committed or redistributed.
	  The ordinary B06V7 image and behavior are unchanged when this option is
	  off.

	  Historical warning: the original B06V8 experiment did not enable ICH10
	  RCBA+0x3400 bit 2.  Consequently, ports 0x72/0x73 aliased the standard
	  RTC bank and the claimed extended-CMOS tuple was time-dependent.  Keep
	  this option only to reproduce the recorded B06V8 experiment; use B06V9
	  for the corrected deterministic profile.

config X58_PRO_E_B06V9_DETERMINISTIC_QPI_3PASS
	bool "Enable B06V9 deterministic High-QPI three-pass CSI probe"
	depends on X58_PRO_E_B06V8_HIGH_QPI_3PASS
	default n
	help
	  Correct the B06V8 RTC-bank alias and remove the wrapper's dependence on
	  time-varying CMOS input bytes.  After the existing early ICH10 BAR setup,
	  B06V9 accepts RCBA+0x3400 only as 0 or BIT(2), sets BIT(2), and requires
	  exact read-back before any vendor call.  The local, user-supplied CSI
	  wrapper is hash-pinned and patched at six documented regions so its
	  High-QPI CSI state is deterministic for the exact E5645, sole-SPD-0x54,
	  DDR-ratio-6 experiment.

	  B06V9 retains the B06V8 three-pass I801/CMOS retry guards, exact CPU/IOH
	  state gates, MSI IOH SYRE reset edge, terminal CAR ROMMON, and complete
	  pass-3 telemetry.  It never invokes MINIT or hands off to postcar,
	  ramstage, or a payload.  The patched wrapper and other proprietary bytes
	  remain local-only and must not be committed or redistributed.

config X58_PRO_E_B06VA_HIGH_QPI_A0_SET
	bool "Enable B06VA observed High-QPI A0-set pass-three probe"
	depends on X58_PRO_E_B06V9_DETERMINISTIC_QPI_3PASS
	default n
	help
	  Extend only the pass-three High-QPI read-only predicate for CPU function
	  ff:02.1 register 0xa0.  B06V9 accepted only 0x00017600 from the first
	  successful post-SYRE target observation.  A controlled B06V9 run and the
	  vendor-booted ratio-6 reference both instead reported 0x00017000 while
	  every decisive CPU/IOH High-QPI endpoint predicate matched.  B06VA accepts
	  exactly those two observed values; it does not mask unknown bits or write
	  this register.

	  All B06V9 wrapper hashes, deterministic state, RTC upper-bank checks,
	  three-pass I801/CMOS guards, MSI IOH SYRE reset edge and terminal CAR
	  behavior remain unchanged.  This option never invokes MINIT and never
	  hands off to postcar, ramstage, or a payload.

config X58_PRO_E_B06VB_HIGH_QPI_MINIT_OBSERVE
	bool "Enable B06VB exact High-QPI MINIT observation"
	depends on X58_PRO_E_B06VA_HIGH_QPI_A0_SET
	default n
	help
	  Extend only the exact B06VA pass-three return observed on the E5645,
	  sole-SPD-0x54, DDR-ratio-6 lab configuration.  B06VB requires the complete
	  CSI-state FNV, the returned 0/0/0x11 tuple, bounded state bytes, final
	  CPU/IOH High-QPI endpoint, memory-clock tuple and stable IOH stage
	  fingerprint.  CPU-link pointer/stage residues are telemetry only.

	  After separately recording that result as a High-QPI observation, B06VB
	  constructs the deterministic invalid-CMOS policy, applies the seven
	  already reviewed byte edits, installs exact FNV 0x3c0f3a0b, and invokes
	  MINIT once in the same CAR context.  A distinct complemented I801 marker
	  plus CMOS 0x0e value 0xec prevents an unexpected reset from repeating the
	  call.  Any returned workspace, runtime and endpoint state is reported
	  observationally and retained for ROMMON inspection.

	  B06VB never accesses ordinary DRAM, never declares training successful,
	  never clears its automatic retry guard, and never hands off to postcar,
	  ramstage, or a payload.  The locally composed proprietary modules remain
	  hash-pinned, private research inputs and are not redistributed.

config X58_PRO_E_B06VC_HIGH_QPI_A0_4SET_MINIT
	bool "Enable B06VC four-value High-QPI A0-set MINIT observation"
	depends on X58_PRO_E_B06VB_HIGH_QPI_MINIT_OBSERVE
	default n
	help
	  Extend only the read-only pre-pass-three CPU ff:02.1 register 0xa0
	  predicate used by B06VB.  Four independent G3 sequences reached the
	  otherwise exact High-QPI endpoint with 0xa0 values 0x00017a00,
	  0x00017800, 0x00017a00, and 0x00017a00.  B06VC therefore accepts exactly
	  the four observed values 0x00017000, 0x00017600, 0x00017800, and
	  0x00017a00 before the third CSI call.  It uses neither a mask nor a
	  numeric range and never writes this register.

	  The post-CSI B06VB observation gate remains unchanged and still requires
	  CPU 0xa0=0x00017000, CSI-state FNV 0x8b38506a, the exact 0/0/0x11 return
	  tuple, and every other recorded state predicate.  Policy construction,
	  the one-shot MINIT guard and call, complete-buffer telemetry, terminal
	  CAR behavior, and the manual-vendor-call lock are inherited unchanged.
	  B06VC never accesses ordinary DRAM and never hands off to postcar,
	  ramstage, or a payload.

config X58_PRO_E_B06VD_HIGH_QPI_CSI2A6_MINIT
	bool "Enable B06VD paired CSI-byte-2a6 High-QPI MINIT observation"
	depends on X58_PRO_E_B06VC_HIGH_QPI_A0_4SET_MINIT
	default n
	help
	  Extend only B06VC's read-only pre-pass-three CPU ff:02.1 register
	  0xa0 predicate and its exact post-CSI state-digest contract.  B06VD
	  admits the additional independently observed pre-pass-three value
	  0x00017c00, yielding the finite exact set 0x00017000, 0x00017600,
	  0x00017800, 0x00017a00, and 0x00017c00.  It uses neither a mask nor a
	  numeric range and never writes this register.

	  At the pass-three return, state byte 0x2a6 and the raw state digest are
	  accepted only as the observed pairs 0x08/0x03e3d24e or
	  0x0c/0x8b38506a.  Both must also produce canonical FNV-1a 0x908dabb6
	  when, solely in the digest stream, offset 0x2a6 is treated as zero.  The
	  raw CSI buffer is never changed.  Every ABI, sparse-byte, canary,
	  pointer/stack and final platform predicate remains mandatory; notably
	  post-CSI CPU 0xa0 remains exactly 0x00017000, CPU 0x9c remains
	  0x00b00502, CPU 0x6c remains 0x0040a0a8, and IOH 0xc8 remains
	  0x0616fc00.  Thus the B06VC run with post-CSI 0xa0=0x00017a00 and
	  0x9c=0x00a00502 still fails closed.

	  Policy construction, one-shot persistent MINIT guard, observational
	  return logging, terminal CAR ROMMON, and the manual-vendor-call lock are
	  inherited unchanged.  B06VD never accesses ordinary DRAM and never
	  hands off to postcar, ramstage, or a payload.

config X58_PRO_E_B06VE_HIGH_QPI_AUTO_HANDOFF
	bool "Enable B06VE exact High-QPI automatic RAM-init handoff"
	depends on X58_PRO_E_B06VD_HIGH_QPI_CSI2A6_MINIT
	default n
	help
	  Promote only the single B06VD High-QPI MINIT return which has direct
	  volatile-memory evidence.  The shared B06VD pair and endpoint gates run
	  first, but only CSI byte 0x2a6=0x08 with raw state FNV-1a 0x03e3d24e may
	  be accepted or authorize MINIT.  The independently observed 0x0c/
	  0x8b38506a pair remains a diagnostic fallback to the CAR ROM monitor.

	  A returned MINIT call must match the exact raw workspace FNV-1a
	  0x94299f43, completion bytes, complete High-QPI/one-channel Uncore
	  endpoint, vendor-stack ABI relationship, and all CAR canaries.  A
	  separate post-MINIT vendor gate requires the observed IOH 00:14.1
	  register 0x9c value 0xbf000000; the pre-MINIT 0xea000000 predicate is not
	  reused after MINIT.

	  On an exact return, the existing B06V6 post-memory path first checks the
	  UC MTRRs, the simultaneous 14-address alias set, both complete 8-MiB
	  scratch windows, and a read-back-verified version-3 CBMEM handoff.  Only
	  after every one of those checks passes are the I801 phase signature and
	  standard CMOS byte 0x0e restored to their exact clear/0x2c values.  Any
	  mismatch keeps the persistent guard armed and falls back or stops.

	  This remains a default-off, fixed E5645/sole-SPD-0x54, locally
	  vendor-assisted experiment.  It is not native X58 memory initialization
	  and does not enable normal PCI enumeration, graphics, or a payload.

config X58_PRO_E_B06VF_SEABIOS_ENTRY
	bool "Enable B06VF minimal SeaBIOS entry probe"
	depends on X58_PRO_E_B06VE_HIGH_QPI_AUTO_HANDOFF
	depends on PAYLOAD_SEABIOS
	default n
	help
	  Continue beyond the B06VE High-QPI, MINIT, DRAM-test, CBMEM, postcar,
	  and ramstage gates only far enough to load and enter a deliberately
	  reduced SeaBIOS 1.17.0 payload.  The payload keeps serial and CBMEM
	  diagnostics but omits PCI BIOS services, drives, USB, option ROMs,
	  graphics helpers, and the boot interface.  It is an entry probe, not a
	  disk-, graphics-, or operating-system boot claim.

	  Accept only the two observed post-MINIT workspace hashes and their
	  coupled byte tuples: 0x94299f43 with 00:00:00:00/fe, or 0xb6346533
	  with ff:ff:ff:ff/ff.  Both must canonicalize to 0xa6f9c2e6.  Before
	  CBMEM, destructively verify and clear the complete 0-640-KiB payload
	  RAM window.  In ramstage, verify the CPU SAD identity, open every PAM
	  half-window with exact readback, and test/restore distinct endpoints
	  throughout C0000-FFFFF before the SELF loader writes SeaBIOS there.

	  Any failed prerequisite retains the existing diagnostic path.  Once
	  SeaBIOS is entered it may perform conventional legacy PIT, DMA, CMOS,
	  and read-only PCI-discovery accesses despite the reduced feature set.
	  This
	  remains a default-off experiment for the exact fixed E5645/sole-SPD-0x54
	  configuration and the locally composed, hash-pinned vendor-assisted
	  initialization path.

config X58_PRO_E_B06VG_COUPLED_MINIT_SEABIOS
	bool "Enable B06VG coupled High-QPI MINIT/SeaBIOS experiment"
	depends on X58_PRO_E_B06VF_SEABIOS_ENTRY
	default n
	help
	  Extend only the B06VF pass-three classifier using the controlled B06VF
	  G3 captures.  B06VG adds the exact pre-CSI CPU ff:02.1 register 0xa0
	  value 0x00017400 to the previously observed values 0x00017000,
	  0x00017600, 0x00017800, 0x00017a00, and 0x00017c00.  Two consecutive
	  reads must agree before CSI; no mask, numeric range, or write is used.

	  Two disjoint post-CSI profiles are recognized.  The PRIMARY profile is
	  the unchanged B06VF payload path: pre/post A0 0x00017000, CPU 0x9c
	  0x00b00502, and the CSI 0x08/0x03e3d24e byte/digest pair.  An
	  OBSERVATION profile instead requires one of the other five exact pre-A0
	  values to survive unchanged, CPU 0x9c 0x00a00502, and either exact
	  0x08/0x03e3d24e or 0x0c/0x8b38506a pair.  Crossed pairs and all other
	  combinations fail closed.

	  An OBSERVATION may make one guarded MINIT call so its complete returned
	  state can be measured, but it always stops in the CAR recovery ROMMON.
	  It cannot reach AUTO_READY, ordinary DRAM tests, CBMEM, ramstage, or
	  SeaBIOS.  Only the PRIMARY profile may use the inherited B06VF promotion
	  and reduced SeaBIOS payload.  Persistent CMOS/I801 reset-loop guards,
	  local proprietary-module hashes, and every post-MINIT B06VF gate remain
	  unchanged.

config X58_PRO_E_B06VH_PRIMARY_WORKSPACE_REARM_SEABIOS
	bool "Enable B06VH exact PRIMARY workspace/rearm SeaBIOS experiment"
	depends on X58_PRO_E_B06VG_COUPLED_MINIT_SEABIOS
	default n
	help
	  Promote only the B06VG PRIMARY profile after one guarded MINIT call.
	  In addition to the inherited 0x94299f43/0xa6f9c2e6 and
	  0xb6346533/0xa6f9c2e6 raw/canonical workspace pairs, admit the two
	  exact PRIMARY captures 0xeb15c076/0xc313e060 and
	  0x5fb636d9/0xb3fafec0.  Each raw digest remains coupled to its observed
	  marker and residual bytes; crossed pairs and the OBSERVATION workspace
	  remain terminal.

	  B06VG hardware showed that successful MINIT deterministically transforms
	  the pre-call I801 phase marker 08:64:9b:5c:a3 into
	  08:00:5d:01:a3.  B06VH requires that exact returned tuple and CMOS 0xec,
	  then, only after every PRIMARY result gate passes, safely re-arms the
	  original 08:64:9b:5c:a3 marker with a fresh exact readback.  This lets
	  the inherited post-memory finalizer retain reset-loop protection while
	  the complete low-memory, alias, CBMEM, and object-window tests execute.

	  A successful path may continue through postcar and ramstage into the
	  reduced serial-only SeaBIOS entry probe.  It still provides no graphics,
	  storage, PCI BIOS, or operating-system boot support and remains a
	  default-off, hash-pinned vendor-assisted experiment.

config X58_PRO_E_B06VI_COUPLED_PROFILE_O_SEABIOS
