	  producer still requires intact local-code signatures and CAR canaries,
	  MINIT EAX zero with a self-consistent ABI record, exact policy, all four
	  universal completion bytes, exact I801/CMOS state, SPD identity, and the
	  complete QPI/IOH/memory-controller endpoint.  A distinct broad profile,
	  handoff version 9, and required evidence flag prevent a B06VK consumer
	  from accepting this result.

	  The I801 guard remains deferred until the inherited UC MTRR gate,
	  complete 0--640-KiB test, simultaneous alias test, both complete 8-MiB
	  window tests, CBMEM creation, and handoff readback all pass.  Any earlier
	  failure retains the CAR recovery monitor.  This is an explicitly risky,
	  default-off, fixed-platform, locally vendor-assisted attempt to reach the
	  reduced serial-only SeaBIOS payload; it is not validated DRAM training,
	  general platform support, graphics, storage, or an operating-system boot.

config X58_PRO_E_B06VM_AUTO_PCI_VGA_IPXE
	bool "Enable B06VM selective PCI/VGA/iPXE first-boot experiment"
	depends on X58_PRO_E_B06VL_BROAD_HARD_GATE_SEABIOS
	depends on PCI
	depends on PCI_ALLOW_BUS_MASTER
	depends on PCI_SET_BUS_MASTER_PCI_BRIDGES
	depends on !PCI_ALLOW_BUS_MASTER_ANY_DEVICE
	select HAVE_CONFIGURABLE_RAMSTAGE
	select CONFIGURABLE_RAMSTAGE
	select MINIMAL_PCI_SCANNING
	select CPU_INTEL_COMMON
	select CPU_INTEL_COMMON_TIMEBASE
	select UDELAY_TSC
	default n
	help
	  Continue only from B06VL's exact version-9 handoff into a deliberately
	  selective ramstage PCI/resource experiment.  The alternate devicetree
	  marks only X58 port 00:03.0 and its GF108 VGA function, ICH10R port
	  00:1c.4 and its RTL8168, the eight captured ICH10R UHCI/EHCI functions,
	  and the two captured legacy-IDE SATA functions as mandatory.  Generic
	  probing of X58 internal host functions 00:0d.* through 00:16.* remains
	  forbidden.

	  Every selected function must match its captured ID, class and header
	  shape before standard BAR sizing.  Endpoint-wide bus mastering is a hard
	  Kconfig exclusion; only the two selected PCI bridges receive BME through
	  coreboot's standard bridge-resource path so payload drivers can DMA
	  through them.  Resource allocation is confined to I/O 0x1000--0xffff and
	  MMIO 0xc0000000--0xdfffffff; a post-allocation callback rejects missing,
	  unassigned, overlapping or out-of-aperture resources before decode is
	  enabled.

	  The selected common Intel timebase derives the pinned E5645's invariant
	  TSC from Westmere model 0x2c's fixed 133-MHz BCLK and
	  MSR_PLATFORM_INFO[15:8].  Its nominal ratio 18 rounds to the expected
	  2400 MHz; B06VM does not retain the earlier zero-frequency delay stub.

	  After exact one-DIMM SAD, IOH TOLM/TOHM and PCIEXBAR readback, B06VM
	  publishes the fixed 4-GiB physical RAM map: 1 MiB--3 GiB plus the
	  remapped 4-GiB--5-GiB range.  This bold first-boot experiment assumes
	  that memory outside B06VL's bounded smoke windows is stable; it does not
	  turn that explicit assumption into hardware validation.  B06VL remains
	  unchanged when this option is disabled.

config X58_PRO_E_B06VN_IOU0_PCIE_PHYS_VBIOS
	bool "Enable B06VN IOU0 PCIe-start and physical-VBIOS experiment"
