	  separately selected X58 IOU0 hypothesis.  After B06VM's exact handoff,
	  memory-map, PCIEXBAR and root-identity gates, B06VN writes only the
	  documented PCIE_PRTx_BIF_CTRL start value 0x000c at ECAM address
	  0xe0018190 for root port 00:03.0, and only when Link Status reports that
	  the data-link layer is inactive.  Ports 00:01.0 and 00:07.0 receive
	  read-only PRE/POST telemetry.  No Link Control retrain is requested.

	  Link Status polling is bounded to one second.  A link timeout or absent
	  VGA endpoint is recorded but continues to the serial SeaBIOS path.  A
	  present endpoint must identify as AMD vendor 0x1002 with VGA class and a
	  normal header before BAR sizing; its device ID is observed at runtime,
	  not guessed.  The RTL8168, USB and SATA identities remain mandatory and
	  fail closed.

	  Coreboot does not embed or execute an AMD option ROM.  SeaBIOS may use
	  only the physical VGA ROM exposed by the card, with normal option-ROM
	  checksum validation retained.  The existing CBFS RTL8168 iPXE ROM stays
	  independent of this physical-VBIOS experiment.

config X58_PRO_E_B06VO_IOHBUSNO_ROUTE
	bool "Enable B06VO IOHBUSNO routing-repair probe"
	depends on X58_PRO_E_B06VN_IOU0_PCIE_PHYS_VBIOS
	default n
	help
