	  performs a 16-bit masked MAP update and the mandatory BAR5 clear after
	  its type changes from I/O to memory. The normal PCI allocator may assign
	  the resulting memory BAR later; this helper does not choose an address.
	  Complete MAP/BAR readback, D31:F2 transition to 8086:3a22/010601 and
	  disappearance of D31:F5 are required before PCI scanning. This option
	  does not enable ports, program SATA clocks, access AHCI MMIO, or run the
	  broad ICH10 driver.

config X58_PRO_E_B06VS_ICH10_AHCI_PORTS
	bool "Enable B06VS ICH10 AHCI port-enable selection"
	depends on X58_PRO_E_B06VR_ICH10_AHCI_MAP
	select SOUTHBRIDGE_INTEL_I82801JX_SATA_PORT_ENABLE
	default n
	help
	  Preserve B06VR's exact AHCI-mode transition and complete inherited
	  platform path. After normal PCI enumeration, BAR sizing, allocation and
	  resource storage have all passed their existing fail-closed audits,
	  require D31:F2 to remain exact 8086:3a22/010601 with D31:F5 absent,
	  MAP 0060, and hardware I/O, memory and bus-master command bits clear.

	  Require BAR5 to be an assigned and stored 2-KiB, 32-bit,
	  non-prefetchable memory resource with exactly MEM|ASSIGNED|STORED flags
	  inside the existing PCI MMIO aperture,
	  with its raw BAR matching the allocated base. Then change only
	  PCS[5:0] to 0x3f using an 8-bit low-byte masked read-modify-write as
	  required by ICH10 section 14.1.31. Exact pre-enable values 0x00 and 0x3f
	  are admitted; bits 7:6 and reserved bit 14 must remain zero. The
	  high-byte presence fields are read-only telemetry and are not admission
	  keys, while OOB Retry Mode bit 15 is deliberately preserved.

	  Any partial mode, decode, resource or PCS state halts before device
	  enablement. This option does not change ORM, presence fields, SATA
	  clocks, PI or any AHCI MMIO register, and does not run the broad ICH10
	  driver.

