config X58_PRO_E_B06WG_AUTO_USB_SEABIOS
	bool "Enable B06WG automatic GPIO57 USB release for SeaBIOS"
	depends on X58_PRO_E_B06WE_ACPI_SAD_BDF_FIX
	depends on PAYLOAD_SEABIOS
	depends on !X58_PRO_E_B06WF_USB_LAB
	default n
	help
	  Preserve the complete B06WE SeaBIOS/iPXE platform path and promote only
	  the live-proven GPIO57/H_PWRGD experiment to an automatic, fail-closed
	  late-ramstage action.  After PCI resource assignment and device init, the
	  path requires the measured B06WD control/decode/controller state and live
	  over-current on all twelve EHCI/UHCI port views.  It then drives only the
	  GPIO57 target output-low, waits 65,536 calibrated microseconds, drives it
	  high, and requires every live OCA indication to clear.  Sticky OCC/OCI and
	  asynchronous connection/speed fields are logged but never gate success.
	  To shorten this USB-focused experiment, B06WG alone treats the previously
	  qualified RAM/QPI path as provisionally stable: it retains the exact
	  result and MTRR gates plus the transactional alias smoke, but replaces
	  phase-A/inverted/full-read memory passes with one deterministic clear pass
	  over lowmem, CBMEM and object windows and nine sparse readbacks per window.
	  The serial log labels this weaker admission ASSUMED_STABLE.  Historical
	  images retain their exhaustive memory tests unchanged.

	  A second read-only gate immediately before the payload requires GPIO57 to
	  remain output/high and every live OCA indication to remain clear.  SeaBIOS
	  retains complete ownership of EHCI/UHCI reset, companion routing, USB
	  enumeration and HID setup; this option never writes PCI configuration,
	  USB controller registers or PORTSC.  A failed post-mutation check attempts
	  a decode-revalidated GPIO57 low/input rollback and blocks the payload.
	  This default-off experiment is separate from B06WF's interactive lab and
	  requires the socketed-flash and one-second AC recovery path.

